<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Luidia sarsii africana">
  <data key="d0">Luidia sarsii africana</data>
  <data key="d1">taxon</data>
  <data key="d2">A starfish taxon in the family Luidiidae, order Paxillosida, class Asteroidea, phylum Echinodermata; common name Legs break easily starfish; arms break off easily, distinct spines on aboral margin, long flexible flattened tapering arms, usually five; colour brown to dark pink; size up to 150 mm diameter; distribution Southern African endemic along West and South Coasts of South Africa to Port Elizabeth at 54-360+ m depth; similar to Astropecten polyacanthus and Astropecten exilis but with more flattened broader arms and easy arm breakage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e079ae16950de487467ccdcc018dc76d</data>
  <data key="d4">Field-Guide-to-SA-Offshore-Marine-Invertebrates_web-full-version_compressed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1789380570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
